05/01/26

Current Databank file format:                             One Byte
                                                            |                  |---[int payload]
    [[Magic][Version][Latest ID]] -> [End of row offset][Datatype] ------------|
            Header = 12 bytes           |                                      |
            ID at Byte 8.               [So that you know when the row ends]   |---[String len][String payload] 

Current ID index file format:

    [[Magic][Version][type]] -> [Value][offset] -- > Always 4 + 4 bytes wide.
        Header = 12 bytes
        Type = always 1 byte

    Formila for getting the id you want:

        int id_location_offset = (ID - 1) * 8;
        where ID is the id you want to fetch, -1 is because the index always starts at 0 and 8 is the 
        size of each record.

    This jumps directly to the id, so no binary seach tree needed, its the fastest way to fetch a row
    as it is O(1).

Current MetaData file format:

    [[Magic][Version]] -> [len][Table name] -> [Number of Columns] -> [Type] -> [len][column name]

    Header = 8 bytes
    Type = 1 byte

Cureent BST Secondary (value) index file format:

    [[Magic][Version][type]] ----int----> [Value][offset][overflow offset][right pointer][left pointer]
                             |              
                             ----str----> [len][value][overflow offset][right pointer][left pointer]
                             |
                             ----double-> [Value][offset][overflow offset][right pointer][left pointer]
    
        Header = 12 bytes
        int value = 4 bytes
        len(uint34_t) = 4 bytes
        str value = len
        double value = 8 bytes
        offset = 4 bytes
        pointers (overflow offset, right pointer, left pointer) = 4 bytes

        Note: overflow offset is for recording the location of due values (keys) in a linked list.